 Step 1: Distribute the 6 to both terms inside the parentheses.
\begin{align*}
(1+2i)6-3i &= 6(1+2i)-3i \\
&= 6 \cdot 1 + 6 \cdot 2i - 3i \\
&= 6 + 12i - 3i
\end{align*}
Step 2: Combine the like terms (the real parts and the imaginary parts separately).
\begin{align*}
6 + 12i - 3i &= 6 + (12i - 3i) \\
&= 6 + 9i
\end{align*}
The final answer is \boxed{6 + 9i}.
